Original commit body from 6af04fb895bcccd83eea6fd498b642a9a133a4c8:

sketch and compact both advertise "the important symbols" and both already
ranked with compute_dampened_centrality -- the 2026-07-09 default flip
settled the ranking FUNCTION -- yet their top-10 lists disagreed. The cause
was never the ranking. sketch filtered to key declaration kinds over
test-source-free edges; compact's default select_by_coverage filtered
nothing at all.

The policy that made sketch's list good was a frozenset declared INSIDE
sketch._format_symbols, with its four clauses as an inline comprehension
beneath it, reachable by nothing else. There was no shared definition to
drift from -- only one function's private opinion. KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS,
is_key_symbol, key_symbols and production_edges now live in
selection/filters.py, the module whose own header already named sketch,
compact and tiered JSON as its consumers.

MEASURED through the production entry points on both sides, on the eight
2026-07-17 bakeoff maps: top-10 agreement 31.2% -> 55.0%, and at the
shipped default budget of 100, 42.8% -> 73.0%. 8/8 repos improved or held
at K=10, 8/8 improved at K=100 (SwiftyJSON 16.7 -> 100, express 18 -> 74.7,
sherpa-csharp 25 -> 76.1). The 31.2% before-figure independently reproduces
the 32% the item recorded.

The EDGE filter is the dominant clause, which is the opposite of the
obvious guess: against sketch's ranked top-10, the symbol filter alone
reaches 7.1/10, the edge filter alone 8.4/10, both together 10/10 on all
eight. compact had been crediting symbols for being called by their own
test suites. That is why both clauses apply and why a denylist-only variant
-- which would have subsumed WI-fadab -- was rejected at 9.4/10 with two
repos missed.

Scope held deliberately. --connectivity is exempt and keeps the broader
population: its contract is bridging disconnected components and a file
node is often the only thing joining two islands, so narrowing it would
remove the bridges the mode exists to find (pinned by an over-reach guard).
Narrowing runs before seed extraction rather than at the ranking call, so
it also constrains force-inclusion -- which is the point, since a seed that
is not a key symbol is exactly the noise leading compact today
(sherpa-csharp's top five were all run*.sh file nodes). `variable` sits in
both KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS and EXCLUDED_KINDS and stays in both: a Terraform
variable is a real declaration surface, a CSS custom property is zero-edge
noise, and which set a consumer applies is its own policy choice.

RESIDUAL, stated rather than implied: 55%, not 100%. With the population
shared the ranked orders match exactly; what remains is that the two use
different SELECTION policies over that shared ranking -- compact reserves
half its budget for entrypoint and cross-cutting seeds, sketch uses
two-phase coverage-first selection with per-file caps. Separate design
difference, not a filter divergence; WI-zulij still tracks it.

Two of the three new property tests were VACUOUS on first draft and are
documented as such in place: one passed because the coverage stop had
truncated the selection to a single symbol, the other because its fixture
used `calls`, a CROSS_CUTTING_EDGE_TYPES member, so every endpoint became a
seed candidate and the ranking under test was never exercised. Both now
carry explicit non-vacuity assertions. The sketch extraction is
behavior-preserving, pinned by its existing 526 tests passing unchanged.

